@page "/teen-bible-quiz"

<PageTitle>TeenBibleQuiz.com - Collyn Brenner</PageTitle>

<ProjectsPageTemplate>
    <article class="project-info">
        <h1>TeenBibleQuiz.com</h1>
        <p class="project-meta">
            Website:
            <a href="https://teenbiblequiz.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">TeenBibleQuiz.com</a>
            <br />
            GitHub Branch:
            <a href="https://github.com/CCBrenner/TBQNextApp" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">/CCBrenner/TBQNextApp</a>
        </p>

        <p>
            TeenBibleQuiz.com is "your all-in-one headquarters for all things Bible Quizzing." It introduces teen Bible
            quizzing, "the sport you've never heard of, until now," to people discovering it for the first time, and
            gives teams, coaches and quizmasters a single place to find what they need. I have been its author and
            maintainer since 2024, carrying on the work of its previous owner, David Phillips, and rebuilding it as a
            Next.js app.
        </p>
        <p>
            For newcomers, a four-part "Intro to Quizzing" series walks through quiz rounds, Scripture portions, quiz
            meets and quiz practice. Supporting pages cover the question types, the eight-year Scripture portion
            rotation, the different types of quizzing and the equipment each one uses, while videos and testimonies
            show what quizzing looks like and what it means to the people involved.
        </p>
        <p>
            For those ready to get involved, the site explains how to create a team, which takes just one adult and a
            few interested teens, including practical ways to get quiz equipment. Its Team Finder helps people find a
            team nearby, and teams can add themselves to its list and map. Directories of Nazarene quizzing districts
            and of quizzing organizations across many denominations, along with an overview of district, field and
            national events, help families and leaders connect with the right people.
        </p>
        <p>
            For teams already quizzing, the Resources page gathers rulebooks, printable scoresheets, study materials,
            memorization tools and question set sources in one place. The site also includes Quizmaster's Queue (QQ), a
            tool that lets a quizmaster upload a question set generated from Set Maker and step through the questions
            right in the browser.
        </p>
    </article>
</ProjectsPageTemplate>

@code { }
